    "tip": "If asked what should be recorded in a log, list the aim and plan, changes to the plan and why, raw data and observations (including unexpected ones), calculations, sources, problems and reflections. Then give two reasons for keeping one, such as evidence of what was done, honesty and integrity, or letting the work be repeated or written up."
